#d	Khmer–English, as complete as open sources make it: every Khmer word they give English for, with all they say of it. Its English by sense, machine-made (Bibles, OPUS and NLLB word-aligned with eflomal; the senses English Wiktionary’s and Open English WordNet’s, told apart by the sentences, other languages’ Bibles, ALT and the Bible’s Greek and Hebrew; checked against Headley’s and Chuon Nath’s dictionaries, not quoted), an example from openly licensed sources; <a href="https://en.wiktionary.org/">English Wiktionary</a>’s entry and translation tables (via <a href="https://kaikki.org/">Kaikki</a>); <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/">Wikidata</a> (CC0); the Greek and Hebrew words the Khmer Bibles translate by it (STEPBible’s tagged texts, CC BY 4.0); its parts under their sources’ licences: <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">CC BY-SA 4.0</a> (Wiktionary’s), CC0 (Wikidata’s). Machine-made parts unchecked: verify before relying on them.
